    "body": "Part of #204. Binding acceptance: https://github.com/nicolas-found42/chief-of-staff-demo/issues/204\n\nUse the records from the foundation ticket to collect and organise actual dossier content, replacing snippet-only name/role extraction as the ceiling of Person Profiles.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Use existing public search and source collection paths; retrieve full available material, retain it, and label snippets, failures, unsupported formats, and incomplete coverage accurately.\n- Start from Identity Signals; iterate using newly supported names, employers, handles, sites, and named work. Follow relevant work and supporting sources within an explicit finite scope. Do not recursively research every collaborator.\n- Extract grounded work/contribution/authority/scale/constraint/outcome records, career transitions, writing and arguments, connections, recognition, attribution, governance, current context, and observed activity dates covering all twenty rows in #204.\n- Validate claimed quotations against retained documents. Unmatched identities and copied-source counts cannot establish factual support. Untrusted source text cannot alter instructions or invoke collection tools outside the allowed research scope.\n- Produce sourced section accounts and an Overview from detailed records without replacing them. Label interpretations and keep unknown, historical, stale, and conflicting claims distinct.\n- Stronger matched evidence may supersede manual factual corrections with an auditable reason and relevant effective dates; mere retrieval recency cannot. Preserve corrections and opposing evidence. Standing wrong-person/rejection decisions remain binding.\n- Incremental extraction preserves useful completed material through partial provider/model failures, source revisions, and repeated collection. Maintain public versus private evidence lineage for every interpretation.\n\nVerification: fixture dossiers for same-name people, conflicting roles, self-reported versus demonstrated skills, team versus personal scope, failures, post-departure outcomes, private evidence, and repeated collaborators; injection/citation tests; declared bounds and partial failure tests.\n",
