    "body": "Part of #204. Binding acceptance: https://github.com/nicolas-found42/chief-of-staff-demo/issues/204\n\nImplement one durable background research interface used by every Profile entry point. Keep scheduling and provider work out of UI requests and preserve progressive results.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Persist queued/running/paused/incomplete/failed/finished-within-scope work, trigger reasons, checkpoints, source/claim progress, allowances, and retry information. Coalesce requests for the same active Profile.\n- Resume finite interrupted work after restart. Guard against duplicate concurrent work and stale in-flight publication after Profile corrections, merge, archive, detach, or privacy deletion.\n- Enforce configurable Workspace pause, concurrency, per-profile work/time, and daily usage limits before dispatch. Count failed attempts, preserve completed work, and distinguish limits from no evidence/source unavailable.\n- Reuse shared search cooldowns; bounded individual requests and retries cannot become unlimited work. Stop dispatch on shutdown and migration gate; prohibit late writes after deletion/gate changes.\n- Provide enqueue/prioritise/pause/resume and read-only progress/control interfaces. Queue priorities support imminent meetings, explicit requests, recently viewed Profiles, and fair backfill.\n- Integrate cancellation and invalidation with every lifecycle operation and Transcript deletion. Source-retention disclosures and privacy deletion receipts remain accurate.\n\nVerification: deterministic clock tests for budget exhaustion/day rollover, crash/resume, deduplication, priority fairness, retry backoff, stop/start/gate behavior, and all in-flight lifecycle races. No detached fire-and-forget promises as the persistence mechanism.\n",
